+
+## Post Studio exports (rule proposed by post-studio Phase 5)
+
+<!-- post-studio-export: allowed -->
+Post Studio (`../post-studio`, Nikola's local design canvas) may write a finished post into `posts/<slug>/`. Only with `pstudio export <project> --to posts/<slug> --social-posts`, and the CLI enforces all of this:
+
+- **Only what Nikola approved.** The revision must be one he approved in the Post Studio editor (the default is `--rev last-approved`). Without an approval it refuses.
+- **Only on-palette posts.** The post must pass its lane's palette check. Post Studio's check gives the same verdicts as `tools/check_palette.py` on real posts (tested in post-studio). It also refuses a post without a brand kit.
+- **Only its own files.** It writes `post.svg`, `post.png`, `post.jpg`, `post-li.*` (a 1080×1350 frame), `figma/*.svg`, `post-studio.json` (the design, so it can be reopened) and `export.json`. It writes `copy.json` only when the folder has none or Post Studio wrote it before. It never touches `brief.md`, captions, `alt.txt`, `review-note.txt` or art sources. A folder with a `post.svg` that Post Studio did not write is refused unless `--force`.
+- **Edit in Post Studio, not here.** A later approved export overwrites `post.*`. Captions and `alt.txt` stay hand-written, as for every post.
+- It only drops files. Posting, poster inboxes and the review-site rebuild stay as described above. Run `python3 review-site/build.py` after an export; a `lux-*` / `kites-*` / `studio-*` folder with `post-studio.json` and `post.jpg` shows up in its lane.
+
+Remove the marker line above to switch exports off again.
